{
  "title": "Occupational Safety and Health Act 1984",
  "abstract": "The Occupational Safety and Health Act 1984 (OSH Act) was the primary workplace health and safety legislation in Western Australia prior to its repeal and replacement by the Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WHS Act) on 31 March 2022. The OSH Act established the foundational framework for workplace safety duties, including the general duty of care obligations for employers to provide and maintain a safe working environment, and for employees to take reasonable care of their own safety and that of others. While now repealed, the OSH Act remains relevant for transitional provisions and understanding the evolution of Western Australian workplace safety regulation.",
